	<body>
		<title>
			<p>Inline pictures</p>
		</title>
		<section>
			<title>
				<p id="title">A title with a photo <image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/> and an icon <image l:href="#icon-16x16.png"/></p>
			</title>
			<epigraph>
				<p id="epigraph">An epigraph with a photo <image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/> in its text.</p>
			</epigraph>
			<p id="alone"><image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/></p>
			<p id="running">Running text before the photo <image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/> and after it, then an icon <image l:href="#icon-16x16.png"/> in the middle of a sentence that goes on long enough to wrap in a narrow window.</p>
			<p id="first-child"><image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/> The paragraph starts with the photo: no indent, and no horizontal scroll bar.</p>
			<p id="icon-alone"><image l:href="#icon-16x16.png"/></p>
			<p id="sup">A superscript picture<sup><image l:href="#icon-16x16.png"/></sup> and a superscript photo<sup><image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/></sup> in the text.</p>
			<p id="note-link">A note link that holds a picture<a l:href="#n1" type="note"><image l:href="#icon-16x16.png"/></a> and one that holds a photo<a l:href="#n2" type="note"><image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/></a>.</p>
			<poem>
				<stanza>
					<v id="poem">A verse with a photo <image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/> in it</v>
					<v>and a verse with no picture.</v>
				</stanza>
			</poem>
			<cite>
				<p id="cite">A cite with a photo <image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/> in its text.</p>
			</cite>
			<table id="cell">
				<tr>
					<td><image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg"/> A picture in a table cell</td>
					<td>The next cell</td>
				</tr>
			</table>
			<p>A block picture follows.</p>
			<image l:href="#photo-572x603.jpg" id="block"/>
			<p id="last">The last paragraph.</p>
		</section>
	</body>
